# Environments — 690 MB and 89 MB. Rebuilt from requirements.txt / package.json.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/

# Build output. Regenerated by `npm run build`.
# Tracked, deliberately, against the usual rule that build output does not
# belong in a repository.
#
# A cabinet needs no JavaScript toolchain — `run.sh kiosk` skips the build when
# `dist` exists, and setup.sh stopped demanding node for exactly this reason.
# The machine this is deployed on has no Node and no administrator password to
# install one, so if the built interface is not in the repository then pulling
# a change updates the source and not one pixel of what anybody sees. Every
# frontend fix would have to be carried by hand, which is how a deployed
# cabinet quietly falls a month behind its own source.
#
# 24 files, 716 KB. The cost is a noisy diff whenever the bundle hash changes.
#
# The footage is the exception: Vite copies `public/` into `dist/` at build
# time, and that is 289 MB of video which is already served from
# `frontend/public/avatars` and mounted ahead of this copy anyway.
frontend/dist/avatars/

# Raw generator downloads. The conformed clips in public/avatars are the source
# of truth; these are the offcuts.
raw/

# Models are downloaded on first run, never committed.
*.onnx

# Not project code.
*.exe
*.zip

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.env

# Signs every studio session token on this machine. Committing it would let
# anyone with the repo mint a valid login for any install built from it.
knowledge/.secret

# The catalog, the knowledge passages and the accounts. A customer's data, and
# rebuilt from their own files by `python -m backend.ingest`.
# The glob matters. This named one filename, and `prune.py` writes
# `catalog.db.bak` beside it — 24 MB holding the `users` table, so every
# customer email and scrypt hash, one `git add -A` from a public repository.
# SQLite's own `-wal` and `-shm` sidecars carry the same rows mid-write.
knowledge/catalog.db*

# A photograph of a real person, uploaded to build a poster. Deleted after the
# cut-out runs; ignored so an interrupted upload never lands in a commit.
frontend/public/avatars/*/source-photo

# Stray personal documents that have collected in avatar folders — invoices,
# scans, passport photographs. An avatar folder holds poster.png, the clips,
# avatar.json and campaigns/, and nothing else. These are somebody's identity and
# financial documents, and this repository gets shared with colleagues.
frontend/public/avatars/*/*.pdf
frontend/public/avatars/*/passport-photo*

# Scratch output from test runs. The suites print to the terminal; these are
# redirections somebody left behind, not artefacts anything reads.
test-*.log

# Written the first time the sample catalog is loaded, so clearing it and
# restarting does not put it back.
knowledge/.seeded

# --- a customer's own content, never ours ------------------------------------
# Avatars, footage, catalogs and seasons belong to whoever installed this. They
# stayed in the repo while it was one showroom and two demo avatars; shipping
# them to a second customer would put Dhiyona's products and our test footage on
# somebody else's panel. A fresh install starts empty and is filled from the
# Studio.
#
# Kept on disk locally — untracked, not deleted — so development still has
# something to talk to.
frontend/public/avatars/
knowledge/products.csv
knowledge/apparel.csv
knowledge/seasons.json
knowledge/kiosks.json
knowledge/events/

# TypeScript incremental build cache. Regenerated by every build, so it
# arrived as a modified file in every single status and diff.
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Written by update.ps1 on the machine it runs on. Machine-local by nature -
# committing it would have every install claiming the same version.
.version

# Written where a snapshot was last applied. Machine-local, like .version.
knowledge/.snapshot-applied

# Written by start.ps1 while it runs. Machine-local and regenerated.
server.log*
tunnel.log*
tunnel-url.txt
cloudflared.exe
